export const TERMS = "# Zome Terms of Service\n\n**Last updated: 13 November 2026**\n\n**Provider:** **Zome Lab Technology Ltd**, a company registered in Nigeria\n(RC 9907281), of Lagos, Nigeria.\n**Contact:** support@myzome.app\n**Governing law:** the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria.\n\nThese terms are an agreement between you and Zome Lab Technology Ltd. By\ncreating a Zome account you accept them. If you do not accept them, do not use\nZome.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Definitions\n\nIn these Terms, the following words have the following meanings, and a defined\nword carries that meaning wherever it appears with a capital letter:\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Account** | The record created when you register to use Zome, identified by your email address. |\n| **Agreement** | These Terms, together with the Privacy Policy, which is incorporated into them by reference. |\n| **Content** | Anything you enter into Zome, including your answers, your food entries, and what you write on a Care Fund. |\n| **Health Data** | Data concerning your physical or mental health, including the data read from Apple Health or Health Connect with your permission, your assessment answers and your Profile. |\n| **Plan** | The Proactive Path generated for you: a sequence of daily goals over a defined period. |\n| **Profile** | Your age band, sex, height, weight, name and nickname. |\n| **Provider**, **we**, **us**, **our** | Zome Lab Technology Ltd, a company registered in Nigeria under number RC 9907281, of Lagos, Nigeria. |\n| **Services** | The Zome apps for iPhone and Android, the web app at app.myzome.app, the website at myzome.app, and any related service we provide. |\n| **you**, **your** | The individual who has accepted this Agreement and holds an Account. |\n\n**1.1** Headings are for convenience and do not affect interpretation.\n\n**1.2** \"Including\" and \"such as\" introduce examples and do not limit what\nprecedes them.\n\n**1.3** A reference to a statute includes any amendment or re-enactment of it.\n\n**1.4** Where this Agreement and the Privacy Policy conflict on the handling of\npersonal data, the Privacy Policy prevails.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What Zome is\n\nZome looks at data your phone already collects about your body, together with\nwhat you tell it, and turns that into a plan for the next 28 days. It scores\nareas of your health — movement, food, recovery, strength and how you are\nfeeling — and suggests one small thing to do each day.\n\nIt is a way of noticing what your own measurements are already saying, and\nacting on it a little at a time.\n\nZome also helps you pay for care. **Care Purse** (§10) keeps money for your\nhealth and pays clinics, pharmacies and labs. **Care Fund** (§11) lets family\nand friends help with a bill that is bigger than the purse.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Zome is not medical care\n\n**This is the most important section in this document. Please read it.**\n\n- **Zome is not a medical device.** It does not diagnose, treat, cure, prevent\n  or monitor any disease, injury or condition.\n- **Zome is not a doctor and does not replace one.** Nothing in the app is a\n  medical opinion about you, and no score is a finding about your health.\n- **Never use Zome to decide whether to seek care.** If something is wrong, see\n  a doctor. If it is urgent, call emergency services. Do not wait for a score to\n  change.\n- **Never change medication, treatment, or a clinician's advice because of\n  anything Zome says.**\n- **Talk to a doctor before starting new exercise or changing what you eat** —\n  particularly if you are pregnant, or have a heart condition, an eating\n  disorder, diabetes, an injury, or any diagnosed condition.\n\nZome's numbers come from data of varying quality: some of it is self-reported,\nand some comes from consumer sensors that are not clinical instruments. Where\nthe app does not have enough evidence to say something, it says so rather than\nguessing. Where it does say something, it is describing your own measurements —\nnot making a finding about your health.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Your account\n\n- You need an account, and the email address you give must be one you control.\n- One account per person. Do not share it.\n- You are responsible for what happens under your account. Keep your password\n  and your device secure.\n- **You must be 18 or over.** Zome is for adults; see the Privacy Policy for\n  why the bar is there and not lower.\n- The first time you sign in on a device or browser we have not seen, we email\n  you a code to check it is you. On the web, you are signed out after 15\n  minutes with nothing done.\n- If you think somebody else has got into your account, tell us at\n  support@myzome.app. You can end every session at once from Profile on the web\n  (Sign out everywhere), or we will do it for you.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Your data\n\nWhat we collect and why is in the [Privacy Policy](PRIVACY-POLICY.md), which\nforms part of these terms.\n\nIn short: your health data is yours. We hold it to run the product for you, we\nnever sell it, no advertiser or insurer ever sees it, and you can delete all of\nit from the iPhone or Android app — Settings → Account → Delete account. That\ndeletion is immediate, permanent and unrecoverable. You can also ask us for a\ncopy of everything we hold about you.\n\n---\n\n## 6. What you may not do\n\n- Use Zome to give anybody else medical advice.\n- Access, or try to access, another person's account or data.\n- Feed the app fabricated data and then rely on the result.\n- Copy, resell, or redistribute the app or its content.\n- Automate access to our API from outside the app, or work around its rate\n  limits.\n- Use Zome to build a competing product, or to train a model on its outputs.\n\nWe may suspend an account being used to do any of these.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Availability\n\nZome is provided as it is. We do not promise it will always be available, that\nit will be free of faults, or that any particular outcome will follow from using\nit. We may change, suspend or discontinue features.\n\nIf we discontinue Zome, we will give you reasonable notice and a way to get your\ndata out before it stops.\n\n---\n\n## 8. What we are responsible for, and what we are not\n\nNothing in this section takes away a right you have by law. If you are a\nconsumer whose rights under Nigerian law say otherwise, that law wins over\nanything written here.\n\n**We do not exclude, and could not exclude, our liability for** death or\npersonal injury caused by our negligence, for fraud, or for anything else the\nlaw does not allow us to limit.\n\n**Subject to that**, and because Zome is provided free of charge:\n\n- We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss: lost profits, lost\n  opportunity, lost data, or the cost of substitute services.\n- We are not liable for any decision you make about your health. Section 2 is\n  the whole of it: Zome is not medical care, and nothing it shows you is a\n  finding about your body. If something is wrong, see a doctor.\n- We are not liable for what other people's services do — Apple Health,\n  Health Connect, your bank, the network your phone is on, the services listed\n  in §14.\n- Where liability cannot be excluded but can be limited, ours is limited to the\n  greater of the amount you have paid us in the twelve months before the claim,\n  or ten thousand naira.\n\n**What we are responsible for** is running the service described here honestly:\nholding your data as the Privacy Policy says we do, not selling it, deleting it\nwhen you ask, and telling you if something goes wrong with it.\n\n---\n\n## 9. What Zome costs\n\nZome is **free** while it is in beta. There is no subscription and no trial\nthat converts. Care Purse (§10) and Care Fund (§11) have their own fees, always\nshown before you pay.\n\nIf that changes, we will tell you in the app before it does, and nothing you\nalready have will start costing money without you choosing it. Any future\nsubscription would be billed through the App Store or Google Play, managed in\nyour account there, and subject to Apple's or Google's terms as well as these.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Care Purse\n\nCare Purse is money you set aside for your health, in the app.\n\n**Who holds it.** Money you add is collected by our licensed payment partners\nand held with a licensed financial institution. Zome keeps the record of how\nmuch of it is yours, and Care Purse shows you that record. Zome is not a bank,\nand Care Purse is not a bank account.\n\n**Checking who you are.** Before you add money to Care Purse or pay from it,\nwe ask you to confirm your BVN or NIN, as the law requires of money services.\nHow much Care Purse can hold, and pay in a day, depends on what you have\nconfirmed; matching a selfie to your record raises those limits. The app shows\nyour limits.\n\n**Adding money by transfer.** The app shows the account to pay into, the\namount to send and the fee, before you pay. The account is for that one\npayment and closes after the time shown.\n\n- **Send exactly the amount shown.**\n- **If you send more**, everything that arrives goes into your Care Purse,\n  less the fee.\n- **If you send less**, you can send the rest while the account is open. Once\n  it closes, what arrived goes into your Care Purse, less the fee.\n- **A transfer cannot be sent back** to the account it came from, so what\n  arrives always goes into your Care Purse.\n\n**Linking a bank account.** Where it is available, you can link a bank account\nin your own name, so money comes from it when you add money, or on a schedule\nyou set. Your bank approves the link, which can take up to three days. We\nnever take more than the limit you set, and never without your tap or your\nschedule. Stop the schedule or unlink the account in the app at any time.\n\n**Fees.** The fee for adding money, and for any payment out, is shown before\nyou confirm. Zome adds no fee of its own to adding money.\n\n**Interest.** Care Purse earns interest only at the rate shown in the app. If\nno rate is shown, it earns none. A rate can change: the app shows a new rate\nbefore it applies.\n\n**Family link.** You can share a link through which anyone can send money to\nyour Care Purse, without a Zome account. Money that arrives this way is a gift\nfor your care: it pays clinics, pharmacies and labs, but it cannot be taken out\nas cash or sent to a bank account in your own name.\n\n**Spending it.** Care Purse pays for care: clinics, pharmacies and labs on\nZome. You read out your pay code (six digits that work once, for a few\nminutes), or approve a bill the provider sends you. Some payments earn\ncashback, shown when you pay. Nothing leaves without your PIN.\n\n**Paying a bank account.** You can also pay any Nigerian bank account from Care\nPurse with your PIN, for example a clinic that is not on Zome yet. The fee is\nshown before you confirm. After you reset your PIN, payments to bank accounts\nwait 24 hours, in case someone else has got into your email; paying a provider\non Zome still works.\n\n**Records.** Every amount added, paid or taken out is recorded and never\nchanged. If you delete your Zome account after using Care Purse, those records\nare kept, locked away, for as long as the law requires, and at least five years\nafter your account closes. Who they belong to is kept encrypted, and opened\nonly for an audit or when the law requires it. Your health data is deleted as\nfor anyone else.\n\n**Deleting your account** waits until Care Purse holds no money, no payment of\nyours is still arriving, and no bank account is linked.\n\n**If something looks wrong**, write to support@myzome.app. We can find your\npayment without a reference.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Care Fund\n\nA Care Fund is a page where someone raises money from other people for a\npatient's medical care. These terms apply to everyone who starts one\n(the **Organiser**) and everyone who gives to one (a **Giver**). By giving to a\nCare Fund, a Giver accepts this section.\n\n**What Zome is, and is not.** Zome is a technology platform that lets people\nraise money for medical care. Zome is not a bank, a microfinance institution,\na trustee, an insurer or an escrow agent. Gifts are collected, held and paid\nout only through licensed payment service providers regulated in Nigeria.\n\n**Held for care, paid only to medical providers.** Everything given to a Care\nFund is held for the patient's medical care and paid only to the bank accounts\nof hospitals, clinics, diagnostic centres, laboratories and pharmacies that\nZome has verified (**Verified Medical Providers**). Zome never pays money from\na Care Fund to the personal bank account of the Organiser, the patient, a\nfamily member or any other private person.\n\n**Checking providers and patients.** Before a Care Fund opens or pays out,\nZome may check a provider's registration, that it exists where it says, and\nits official bank account, and may confirm the patient's medical situation\nwith the provider.\n\n**Checks on large gifts.** Zome and its payment partners watch for suspicious\nactivity, as Nigeria's anti-money-laundering laws and SCUML's guidelines\nrequire. A single transfer of ₦5,000,000 or more is checked by our payment\npartner before it shows on a Care Fund. A Giver of ₦500,000 or more is asked\nfor their full name and phone number.\n\n**When money is paid.** So that urgent care is never delayed, a Care Fund may\npay a Verified Medical Provider in parts, at any time while the fund is open\nor after it ends.\n\n**A fund that doesn't reach its target.** If a Care Fund ends without reaching\nits target, everything raised, less fees, is still paid to Verified Medical\nProviders for the patient's care.\n\n**Pausing or stopping a fund.** Zome may pause, cancel or stop a Care Fund\nstraight away if we suspect fraud, misrepresentation, falsified medical\nrecords or a breach of these Terms, or if the provider confirms that treatment\ncannot go ahead.\n\n**Refunds from a stopped fund.** If Zome stops a Care Fund and money is left\nin it, that money is returned to Givers:\n\n- **If nothing has been paid to a provider**, each Giver gets back their gift,\n  less the payment partners' fees, which can't be refunded, and less the bank\n  transfer fee.\n- **If part has already been paid to a provider**, each Giver gets back their\n  share of what is left, in proportion to their gift, less the bank transfer\n  fee.\n- **Refunds go to the bank account the gift came from.** If the sending bank\n  didn't pass that account on, our support team will contact the Giver by email\n  or phone to arrange the refund.\n- **A refund under ₦100 can't be sent** by bank transfer, under Nigeria's\n  banking network rules.\n- **Zome is not responsible** for a refund that fails or is delayed because of\n  limits or restrictions on the Giver's own bank account.\n\n**Money left over, or a change in treatment.** If the provider confirms that\nthe final bill is lower than what was raised, or if the patient dies or moves\nto another provider before everything is paid, Zome may either use what is\nleft for verified follow-up care at another Verified Medical Provider, or\nreturn it to Givers as described above.\n\n**What the Organiser promises.** The Organiser promises that every medical\ndocument, patient detail and cost estimate they give is true and unaltered.\nAn Organiser who starts a Care Fund for someone else confirms they have the\npatient's (or their legal guardian's) explicit, informed consent to show the\npatient's name, medical condition, photographs and hospital details publicly\non Zome, as Nigeria's data protection law requires.\n\n---\n\n## 12. How Zome uses AI, and what it is not allowed to do\n\nA language model writes the *wording* of your plan. That is the whole of its\njob.\n\n**It never measures anything.** It cannot compute a score, create an\nobservation, change a confidence figure, or produce a plan that has not already\npassed our own checks. Every number in Zome comes from fixed rules working on\nyour measurements. The model chooses words for decisions those rules have\nalready made.\n\n**What it receives:** the health information needed to word your plan. **What it\nnever receives:** your email or your name. It runs in the United States and\nkeeps nothing it is sent. Our Privacy Policy says more.\n\n**It is not a chatbot and not a clinician.** It cannot give health or medical\nadvice, and Zome does not offer any.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Changes, and leaving\n\n**Changing these terms.** If we change them in a way that affects you, we will\ntell you in the app before it takes effect. Carrying on using Zome after that is\nhow you accept the change; if you would rather not, delete your account.\n\n**Leaving.** Delete your account in the iPhone or Android app: Settings →\nAccount → Delete account. It takes two taps and a check that it is you, and it\nhappens immediately. We\ndo not ask you to email anybody, and we will never make leaving harder than\njoining was.\n\n**What deletion does not reach**, said here because knowing afterwards\nis too late:\n\n- **Apple Health and Health Connect.** Data your phone saved there is your\n  phone's, not ours. Remove it in the Health app on iPhone, or in Health\n  Connect on Android.\n- **Care Purse records**, if you used Care Purse, kept as §10 says.\n- **The fact that a deletion happened.** We keep a dated record with nothing in\n  it that identifies you, because being able to show that we deleted something\n  is part of having deleted it.\n\n**Ending it from our side.** We may close an account that is being used to break\n§6, or where the law requires it. We will tell you why, and give you a way to\nget your data out first unless doing so would be unlawful.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Other people's services\n\nZome depends on services from others, and their terms apply to their part:\n\n| Service | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Apple Health** and **Health Connect** | Supply the data you allow, from your phone |\n| **Sign in with Apple** and **Google** | Let you sign in with those accounts, if you choose |\n| **Open Food Facts** | Supplies nutrient information |\n| Licensed payment partners | Collect and hold Care Purse and Care Fund money, send payments to bank accounts, and link bank accounts |\n| Identity checks | Confirm who you are for Care Purse |\n| Push notifications (Apple and Google) | Deliver notifications to your phone |\n| Hosting, database, storage and email delivery | Run the product |\n\n**Nutrient information comes from Open Food Facts, a public database maintained\nby volunteers. It can be wrong, and we do not verify it.** Treat it as a guide,\nnot a measurement.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Disputes and governing law\n\n**15.1 Talk to us first.** If you have a complaint, write to\nsupport@myzome.app setting out what has happened and what you would like us to\ndo. We will acknowledge within 5 working days and give a substantive response\nwithin 30 days. Most things end here, and neither of us needs a court.\n\n**15.2 Governing law.** This Agreement, and any dispute arising out of or in\nconnection with it, including any non-contractual dispute, is governed by the\nlaws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria.\n\n**15.3 Jurisdiction.** The courts of the Federal Republic of Nigeria have\njurisdiction. **This does not take away a right you have under Nigerian\nconsumer protection law**, including protections that cannot be contracted out\nof.\n\n**15.4 Regulators.** Nothing in this section affects your right to complain to\nthe Nigeria Data Protection Commission. That route is set out in the Privacy\nPolicy.\n\n**15.5 No class actions are waived, and no arbitration is imposed.** We have\ndeliberately not required you to arbitrate or to give up any collective remedy.\n\n---\n\n## 16. General\n\n**16.1 Entire agreement.** This Agreement is the whole agreement between you\nand us about the Services, and replaces anything said or written before it.\nNothing in this clause limits liability for fraud or fraudulent\nmisrepresentation.\n\n**16.2 Severability.** If any provision of this Agreement is found to be\nunlawful or unenforceable, it is severed to the minimum extent necessary and\nthe rest continues in force. Where a provision can be made enforceable by\nnarrowing it, it applies as narrowed rather than being struck out.\n\n**16.3 Waiver.** If we do not enforce a provision, or delay in doing so, that\nis not a waiver of it and does not prevent us enforcing it later. A waiver is\neffective only if we give it in writing.\n\n**16.4 Assignment.** You may not assign or transfer this Agreement or your\nAccount. We may assign this Agreement to a group company, or to a buyer of the\nbusiness or its assets, provided your rights under it are not reduced. We will\ntell you in the app before any such transfer takes effect, and the Privacy\nPolicy sets out what happens to your data.\n\n**16.5 Force majeure.** Neither party is liable for a failure to perform caused\nby something outside its reasonable control, including a failure of the public\ninternet, a power failure, an act of a government or regulator, or an outage at\na supplier named in the Privacy Policy. This does not excuse a failure to\nrefund money owed to you.\n\n**16.6 Notices.** We give you notice through the app or by email to the address\non your Account, and it is treated as received when sent. You give us notice by\nemail to support@myzome.app, and it is treated as received when we acknowledge\nit. Keep your email address current: it is the only way we can reach you.\n\n**16.7 Survival.** Sections 1, 3, 5 and 8, what §10 says about records, what\n§11 says about refunds, and sections 15 and 16 survive the ending of this\nAgreement, together with anything else which by its nature is intended to.\n\n**16.8 No third-party rights.** Nobody who is not a party to this Agreement may\nenforce it.\n\n**16.9 Language.** This Agreement is made in English. Any translation is for\nconvenience, and the English text governs.\n\n**16.10 Relationship.** Nothing here makes either of us the agent, partner or\nemployee of the other.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Contact\n\n**Zome Lab Technology Ltd** (RC 9907281)\nLagos, Nigeria\nsupport@myzome.app · privacy@myzome.app\n"
